From 6d137de6305efb1f6a13274806e8a072e257249c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mike_ding <mike_ding@sercomm.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:14:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stp: fix stack buffer overflow when sending PVST BPDU

STP_MAX_PKT_LEN is 68, but sizeof(PVST_CONFIG_BPDU) is 84 bytes and
stp_pkt_tx_handler() adds 4 more for the VLAN tag => 88 bytes.

stp_pkt_fill_tx_buf() copies the whole packet into the stack array
"char send_buf[STP_MAX_PKT_LEN]", so it wrote up to 20 bytes past the
end of send_buf[]. With _FORTIFY_SOURCE=2 glibc detects this in
__memcpy_chk and kills the daemon:

    *** buffer overflow detected ***: terminated
    exited: stpd (terminated by SIGABRT (core dumped); not expected)

Reproduced on the KaiTian board with a single-port loopback: the crash
happens ~1.5s after the link goes up, i.e. when the first BPDU is sent.
Standard STP BPDUs (72+4=76) overflowed as well, they just never got
sent while ports stayed down.

- raise STP_MAX_PKT_LEN to 256 (also fixes the RX path, which was
  truncating 88 byte PVST frames with iov_len = STP_MAX_PKT_LEN)
- reject oversized BPDUs in stp_pkt_tx_handler() instead of overflowing
---
 include/stp.h | 2 +-
 stp/stp_pkt.c | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/stp.h b/include/stp.h
index 1fba245..14faf14 100755
--- a/include/stp.h
+++ b/include/stp.h
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@
 #define STP_SIZEOF_CONFIG_BPDU 35
 #define STP_SIZEOF_TCN_BPDU 4
 #define STP_BULK_MESG_LENGTH 350
-#define STP_MAX_PKT_LEN 68
+#define STP_MAX_PKT_LEN 256
 
 #define g_stp_instances stp_global.max_instances
 #define g_stp_active_instances stp_global.active_instances
diff --git a/stp/stp_pkt.c b/stp/stp_pkt.c
index 16217fa..14f47ad 100644
--- a/stp/stp_pkt.c
+++ b/stp/stp_pkt.c
@@ -226,6 +226,14 @@ int stp_pkt_tx_handler(uint32_t port_id, VLAN_ID vlan_id, char *buffer, uint16_t
     if (tagged)
         size += VLAN_HEADER_LEN;
 
+    /* never let an oversized BPDU (e.g. PVST, 88 bytes) overflow send_buf[] */
+    if (size > STP_MAX_PKT_LEN)
+    {
+        STPD_INCR_PKT_COUNT(port_id, pkt_tx_err);
+        STP_LOG_ERR("STP-BPDU too large: %u > %d", size, STP_MAX_PKT_LEN);
+        return -1;
+    }
+
     memset(send_buf, 0, STP_MAX_PKT_LEN);
     stp_pkt_fill_tx_buf(size, tagged?vlan_id:0, buffer, send_buf);
 
-- 
2.34.1

